@title PCSA00015 campaign race - boot to a LIVE RACE on the campaign's first event
@game  PCSA00015

# ============================================================================
# WHAT THIS RECIPE DOES
#   boot -> PRESS ANY BUTTON -> GAME MODE -> SINGLE PLAYER CAMPAIGN
#        -> campaign intro -> the campaign MAP -> select the event EMPIRE CLIMB
#        -> event briefing -> START -> SELECT TEAM -> the load -> the pre-race
#        card -> the race is LIVE at f7300.
#
# At the end of this recipe the title is racing: LAP 1/3, POS 8/8, the world
# pass carries several hundred draws, `camera` tracks the ship, and holding `r`
# (thrust) flies it down the track. ZERO shader fallbacks over the whole run.
#
# >>> IT NEEDS `VITASLOP_FRAME_TOPUP=0`, AND THAT IS NOT OPTIONAL.
# With the default per-flip clock top-up a displayed frame carries about a
# TENTH of the guest work a console frame carries, and this title never
# finishes loading at all. See `VitaState::advance_time_frame`.
#
#   VITASLOP_FRAME_TOPUP=0 play --game <dir> --recipe <this> --max-frames 12000
#
# >>> THE MAP NEEDS TWO TAPS IN ONE PLACE, NOT A 35-TAP SWEEP.
# The version of this recipe before 2026-08-06f swept 35 taps across the map
# over 6,800 frames and reached the race at f44,600, and its header insisted
# every tap was load-bearing because the map pans. It does not need to pan. The
# map opens with a "TOUCH TO START" prompt: the first tap dismisses it and the
# second selects the node under it. MEASURED - two taps at (1000,550) and the
# EMPIRE CLIMB briefing is up 100 frames later.
#
# >>> EVERY FRAME BELOW IS MEASURED, one headless GPU run per step, shots every
# 100 frames:
#   f1100  title, PRESS ANY BUTTON TO START
#   f1400  GAME MODE
#   f2100  campaign intro
#   f3100  campaign MAP
#   f3900  EMPIRE CLIMB briefing (RACE, NO WEAPONS)
#  ~f4400  SELECT TEAM (only FEISAR SPEED is unlocked)
#   f4300-f5600  the CONTROLS/RACER legend with LOADING 0% -> 100%
#   f5700-f7200  the track flyby behind the RACE card
#   f7300  THE RACE IS LIVE
# Judge a live race by the HUD (LAP/POS/TOTAL), never by a world scene: the
# flyby that plays over the load is a world scene and reads exactly like one.
#
# >>> THE GESTURE TYPE MASK MATTERS AND THE DEFAULT IS NOW RIGHT
# SceSystemGesture recognizers come in types 1/2/4/8 and their meanings are not
# published. Reporting a touch to ALL of them tells the title a tap and a drag
# and a pinch happened at once, and the map then only ever PANS - no tap
# selects anything. Type 1 alone selects. `vita::gesture::type_mask` now
# defaults to 1 for that reason; `VITASLOP_GESTURE_TYPE_MASK=15` reproduces the
# old behaviour and this recipe then reaches the map and stops there.
#
# >>> THE MAP RENDERS AS A WHITE HEX LATTICE, AND THAT IS A KNOWN DEFECT.
# The campaign map's body is drawn by a vertex program that fetches `canvasTex`,
# and it lands in the wrong place - over the whole screen, on every screen from
# f600 on. That is why a node's position cannot be read off a shot and why the
# taps here are blind. When it is fixed, these two taps become one aimed one.
# ============================================================================

0: @section boot
# No input while it loads - this is boot.recipe's ladder, unchanged.

1300: cross
1300: @shot title-screen
1315:
# "PRESS ANY BUTTON TO START" -> GAME MODE.

2000: touch=472,524
2000: @shot game-mode
2015:
# The SINGLE PLAYER CAMPAIGN tile (screen 236,262). ONLINE CAMPAIGN and
# CROSS-PLAY are correctly greyed out (signed out); ADHOC needs a second unit.

3000: touch=1760,952
3000: @shot campaign-intro
3020:
# The intro text ("Touch the nodes to play events") and its confirm checkmark,
# bottom right (screen 880,476).

3200: @section campaign-map
3200: @shot campaign-map

3400: touch=1000,550
3415:
# Dismisses the map's "TOUCH TO START" prompt.

3800: touch=1000,550
3815:
# ...and this one lands on the event node. The title spawns its
# LoadingScreenThread a few frames later
# (`RUST_LOG=vitaslop::thread=debug`), which is the machine-readable signal.

4000: @shot event-briefing
# EMPIRE CLIMB / NO WEAPONS, with the track photo, a ship button, a cancel X
# and a START triangle along the bottom (screen 622/752/881, 480).

4200: touch=1762,960
4220:
# START.

4600: @shot select-team
# SELECT TEAM. Only FEISAR SPEED is unlocked (SPEED 8 / HANDLING 7 / HEALTH 4 /
# FIREPOWER 6); every other hull carries a padlock.

5000: touch=1762,960
5020:
# Its confirm checkmark, same place.

5400: @section event-loading
# The CONTROLS/RACER legend with a LOADING percentage. That legend is where the
# race controls below come from: STEER/PITCH = LEFT STICK, R = THRUST,
# X = FIRE/USE PICKUP, plus airbrake and absorb.

6800: @shot pre-race
# The RACE card over a flyby of the circuit, with a confirm checkmark.

7200: touch=1762,960
7220:

7600: @section race
7600: @shot race-start
# From here the title is in the event: the HUD reads LAP 1/3 POS 8/8, `start`
# opens the in-race GAME PAUSED menu, and the frame is a race frame - a
# 1024x1024 shadow pass, reflection and post targets, and a world pass of
# several hundred draws into an offscreen target that the composite samples.
#
# @note The composite CANNOT be reproduced by the software renderer: its
# fullscreen blit carries no texcoord attribute (the shader derives the UV), so
# `play`'s `@shot` here is the HUD over black - which is exactly what makes it
# the right oracle for LAP/POS/TOTAL. For the world, render through
# `vitaslop-desktop --headless` with VITASLOP_GXP_LIVE=1.
#
# @todo Drive it, and drive it WELL. The best any controller has managed is one
# lap's worth of distance without the lap counter ever moving. The controller
# that gets furthest follows the seven AI SHIPS - they are on the racing line by
# construction, `locate` reports their world positions directly, and at POS 8/8
# they are all ahead - and it corners far better than the material-fan one it
# replaces, but it is stopped by a wall near (1120, 1780) at the top of the
# first climb, every run, while its aim line passes within 30 units. Render that
# frame through the GPU path before touching the controller again: the failure
# is geometric and no amount of log reading will show what the ship is hitting.
# There is no @assert here until a lap is counted.
12000: @section end
